feat: dashboard injection view and manual attention editing

The reply-suggestions card only showed the guidance block, and the
attention list could only be archived, so there was no way to fix an
item the model mis-recorded without touching data files by hand.

- Rework the guidance card into an "actual injection" view: mood chips,
  body stage, the exact events/attention items select_injected_* picks
  (what the model really sees right now), and the expression guidance.
  The state API now exposes selected_injection_events for it.
- Attention items are editable from the dashboard: a dialog handles
  create and update (content, kind, status, time hint, due date).
  Create goes through observe_attention with a trusted "webui" source;
  update goes through a dedicated mutate callback because the standard
  update branch cannot clear an existing due_at with an empty value.
- The webui source skips the anti-hallucination heuristics (past dates,
  short-lived phrasing): a human typing in the dashboard is the
  authority. Model-path guards are untouched.
